<example scenario="Severely damaged source - heavy restoration required">
<user_input>
PM: "Need to catalog this urgently: /tmp/old_product.jpg"
[You see: Extremely dark underexposed photo, heavy yellow color cast, visible noise grain, product barely discernible - appears to be a leather wallet]
</user_input>

<your_reasoning>
ULTRATHINK: This is a RESCUE operation - source image has multiple severe issues:
1. Underexposed by ~3 stops - shadows crushing product details
2. Heavy yellow/tungsten color cast - will contaminate leather color
3. High ISO noise grain - will destroy texture detail
4. Motion blur on edges - will affect sharpness

Professional assessment:
- This needs FULL restoration: exposure correction, color neutralization, heavy denoise, detail restoration
- Leather material is forgiving for restoration but texture is critical
- May need multiple passes - first restore, then process to base asset
- Flag quality risk to PM but attempt rescue
</your_reasoning>

<your_action>
**PHASE 1: Assess Damage**
view_image("/tmp/old_product.jpg")
-> Confirmed: Severely underexposed leather wallet, yellow cast, grain visible, some motion blur
-> Product identifiable: Bifold wallet, brown leather, appears to have stitching detail

**PHASE 2: Heavy Restoration + Base Asset**
image_studio(
  operation="edit",
  source_image="/tmp/old_product.jpg",
  custom_instruction="RESTORATION + BASE ASSET - EMERGENCY QUALITY RESCUE: Brown leather bifold wallet. SOURCE IMAGE SEVERELY DAMAGED - requires aggressive correction: 1) EXPOSURE: Boost by +2.5 to +3 stops - product is severely underexposed, 2) COLOR: Neutralize heavy yellow/tungsten cast while preserving natural brown leather tone, 3) NOISE: Apply aggressive denoise - source has high ISO grain that will destroy texture, 4) MOTION BLUR: Use AI detail restoration to recover edge sharpness, 5) After restoration: pure white #FFFFFF infinity background, LEATHER material - preserve grain texture and stitching details that survive restoration, HIGH sharpness on stitching and fold lines, subtle contact shadow, 1K quality. WARNING: This is a rescue operation - quality ceiling limited by source damage.",
  background={"type": "solid", "color": "#FFFFFF"},
  lighting={"type": "studio", "direction": "front", "intensity": "high", "color_temperature": "neutral", "shadows": "soft"},
  enhancement={"sharpness": "high", "color_correction": True, "denoise": True, "restore_details": True, "brightness": "high", "contrast": "medium"},
  framing={"product_coverage_percent": 75, "padding_percent": 12, "alignment": "center"},
  output={"format": "PNG", "size": "1K", "aspect_ratio": "1:1", "quality": 95}
)

**PHASE 3: Quality Assessment**
view_image("/tmp/wallet_restored.png")
-> Results:
   - Exposure recovered - product now visible and well-lit
   - Yellow cast neutralized - brown leather looks natural
   - Noise reduced significantly - some texture preserved
   - Edge sharpness improved but not perfect (source limitation)
   - Usable for catalog but not premium quality
</your_action>

<expected_output>
"Professional assessment: EMERGENCY RESTORATION - Severely damaged source image.

Source issues identified:
- Underexposed by ~3 stops
- Heavy yellow color cast
- High ISO noise grain
- Slight motion blur

Restoration applied:
- Exposure boosted +2.5 stops
- Color neutralized while preserving leather brown
- Aggressive denoise with texture preservation
- AI detail restoration on edges

Result: /tmp/wallet_restored.png
- Background: Pure white #FFFFFF
- Material: Leather grain texture partially recovered
- Sharpness: Acceptable (limited by source damage)
- Format: 1K PNG 1:1

QUALITY WARNING: This is a rescue operation. Result is catalog-usable but NOT premium quality. Recommend re-shooting this product for hero imagery if possible. Current output suitable for secondary listing images."
</expected_output>
</example>

